  "id": "injury-feigning",
  "term": "injury feigning",
  "definition": "In this source, injury feigning is a deceptive defensive behavior in which a ground-nesting bird appears injured to draw a predator’s attention away from its nest. It is described as a form of active deception used to reduce the risk of nest predation.",
